model {
  extend basalt.productionOps {
    metadata {
      constraint "Retained inventory captures organization-owned associations for every active, inactive and configured version with database identity in one read-only SQL snapshot, closes that transaction, then resolves only those captured build IDs through R2 without a SQL requery. Its R2 deadline is the smaller of 18 seconds and the remaining unchanged 25-second operation budget after reserving 2 seconds for protection and response; multiple SQL statements do not share an assumed 5-second total. All metadata pages, records, retry attempts and waits consume that one phase deadline. Only closed transient R2 read failures retry, up to three 3-second attempts with bounded 100/200-millisecond waits and 0-20 percent jitter. Completed pages never restart. Each body attempt reserves its full byte allowance, retaining the debit on failure; success and confirmed absence alone refund unused bytes. Native cancellation never awaits the provider promise, and interruption starts no retry. Permanent access failures, malformed records, cursor and byte bounds remain final. Closed object-class, read-phase, measured elapsed-time and bounded aggregate work counts survive phase wrappers, the safe HTTP receipt and the standalone Node operator error and step summary; native messages, object keys and paths never enter those diagnostics."
    }
  }
}
